# Visual acceptance harness (scripts/qa/).
# Accepted captures live in docs/qa/ and ARE tracked — that is the whole point of
# the harness, so nothing here may ignore them. Everything below is scratch: it is
# regenerable, machine-local, or was rejected, and none of it is evidence.
# .qa-cache/ holds vendored React + webfont bytes, fetched once so runs go offline.
.qa-cache/
# .qa-scratch/ is the sink for exploratory and diagnostic runs.
.qa-scratch/
docs/qa/**/rejected/
docs/qa/**/retry-*/
docs/qa/**/diagnostic-*/
docs/qa/**/*.rejected.png

# .qa-quarantine/ is the one exception to "none of it is evidence" above: this IS
# evidence. It holds frames that differed from their baseline, kept as the exact bytes
# the comparison read, because a nondeterministic raster event cannot be re-observed —
# a later render is a new observation, not custody of the original. Untracked because
# it is working evidence rather than an accepted board state; a frame becomes a
# committed fixture only through the founder-ruling path. Never clear one to go green.
.qa-quarantine/

# D1 import output. The report carries governed Wave 0 capture content, which
# lives outside this repository and never becomes a tracked artifact inside it.
# This repository is public; the record is not.
.d1-import/
